What is an Operator in Java?
An operator is a special symbol used to perform operations on variables and values.

Java Operators
Arithmetic :- + - * / %
Relational :- == != > < >= <=
Logical :- && || !
Assignment :- = += -= *= /=
Unary : -++ -- + - !
Bitwise :- & | ^ ~
Shift :-<< >> >>>
Ternary :- ? :

Ex:--
int a = 10;
int b = 20;
int sum = a + b;
System.out.println(sum);

What is Input/Output in Java?
Input/Output (I/O) is the process of taking data from the user and displaying the result to the user.
- Input: Receiving data from the user.
